vil scientist and  planning genetic diseases in people  and it was you know it didn't do that  well but it was good enough to get me a  second book  which was a book called reaper which  none of you heard of that one either  and uh that was about a computer virus  that makes the jump to the biological  world and people  start getting sick from their television  sets and i came up with this idea while  watching oprah  actually um i can say that because the  odds of me getting on oprah are really  small so  um so that that idea was sort of just  trashy enough to catch the attention of  hollywood  and that actually became a tv movie  called fatal error  which still airs on the sci-fi channel  at about  two in the morning and if you see it you  should turn the channel because it stars  antonio sabato jr  if you remember him he was a underwear  model from melrose place and calvin  klein  and he plays a surgeon which was really  believable  casting and uh i remember watching the  movie with my dad who was a doctor  and uh in the middle of it you know  antonio junior leans over this  patient's chest and he goes we've got a  subdural hematoma  and my dad turns me and goes you know  that's in the head right  so that was the level of that movie and  i learned sort of the first rule of  hollywood which is that  the writer ranks just below the caterer  because uh even at the end of the movie  i couldn't get into the wrap party  and i actually had to only get in as  antonio sebato junior's  a part of his entourage so you know it  shows you where the writer ranks in  hollywood  i went on from there and i caught the  attention of the x-files  and they had seen fatal error and i  guess they liked it so they asked me to  come write for the x-files  but i didn't want to move to la because  i at the time i didn't know how to drive  um because you're in boston you don't  really know have to know how to drive  and uh my wife is sitting there she'd  tell you i still don't know how to drive  but i think i'm much better now  but anyways i i said i don't want to  move there but i'll write a book  starring mulder and scully so they said  okay go ahead so i wrote an x-files  novel um starring mulder and scully and  it  takes place mostly in thailand which i  had never been to and i actually just  used a guidebook  to write all the thailand scenes and it  was a about a skin transplant gone bad  and all these people were you know  getting killed by this guy who had  gotten a skin transplant from a murderer  so mulder and scully are investigating  the skin and where it came from  and the book was called skin so it shows  you how creative i am and uh  went on from there and i was really just  looking for another thriller idea  and uh i had no intention of doing  non-fiction and i used to hang out at a  bar called crossroads which a lot of you  probably know crossroads which is  right basically down the street and  there were these mit kids who hung out  there  and they were your regular mit kids i  mean they look like math science guys  and  there was nothing remarkable about them  except for they had tons of money  and it was always in hundred dollar  bills and in boston you really don't see  that many hundred dollar bills  like you know you go to new york you see  hundred dollar bills you go to vegas you  see lots of hundred dollar bills  but in boston you hardly ever see  hundred dollar bills so i went up to the  main guy who in the book i called kevin  lewis  and in the real life his name is jeff ma  now there's a big movie coming out he  wants me to start using his real name  so it's jeff ma um and uh i said jeff  why  why do you have so much money and he  said well come over my house i want to  show you something  so i go over to his apartment and he's  in south end and i go there and he  points to his laundry closet  and i open the closet door and stacked  above his laundry with something like  150  000 in banded stacks of hundred dollar  bills  and 