 two and a half years and  i was blown away by this because i had  been writing these trashy thrillers for  the past two years  and suddenly this was a true story that  was better than any of the stuff i was  coming up with on my own  so i just started following the mit  blackjack team and i started going every  weekend  and i became the money carrier because i  wasn't good enough at math to actually  count cards  so i would strap all the money to my  body it turns out you can carry about a  quarter million dollars under your  clothes pretty easily  and uh you know it's not illegal to  carry your own money but if you get  caught  at logan airport with a quarter million  dollars on you it looks really weird  and yeah you end up in a in a cell  underneath the airport actually  handcuffed  and the dea comes in and the irs comes  in and i don't have to tell you how i  know that but i know that and  you spend some time trying to prove that  it's your money so anyways  basically i started following and a lot  of you probably read bringing down the  house so you know the system where  they'd spread six to ten college kids  out across the casino  one kid sitting at each table and he  would keep track of the cards  and when the cards got good which meant  there were more tens jack kings or  queens or aces in the deck  they would signal the guy called the big  player who's acting like a rich drunk  high roller  and he would walk up to the table and  bet ten thousand dollars a hand  then he'd get the signal it's no longer  good and he would keep walking so in  that way big money was only being placed  down  on good decks and it worked really well  because the casinos couldn't see what  was going on normally it's very easy to  catch a card counter  because you sit there at the table and  you watch the cards and then you double  your bet you triple your bet  the casino sees you doing it there's  nothing illegal about it but they frown  upon it and they'll quickly come and  throw you out or worse um but the mit  team would use this big player system  and they they were doing it very well  they would actually use the casino  stereotypes against them  because the casinos have this view of  what a high roller is supposed to look  like  and if a guy who looks like me comes  into a casino a white guy with glasses  from boston and i come in with a million  dollars it looks really strange  but if an asian kid or a persian kid  comes into a casino  with a million dollars they look like a  high roller so the mit team would  recruit as many asians and persians as  they could which was actually quite easy  to do at mit  and also it turns out that women can get  away with card counting forever  because the casinos don't believe women  can do math  and i interviewed one girl who was an  attractive blonde  who would wear a tennis outfit and she'd  carry a tennis racket and she'd sit at  the blackjack table  and she'd pretend that her husband was  still playing tennis and she was so  bored  and she was an applied economics major  at mit but the assumption was she was a  dumb blonde and she could card count  right in front of everybody and never  get caught  and it also turns out that if there's an  attractive woman in a low-cut outfit  at a casino all of those thousands of  cameras are actually trained on her  and i was actually in the venetian  security booth once and all those  screens  they showed a woman walking through the  casino and sitting down and i said oh is  she going to rob the place  they're like no we just get bored back  here so it's a very sort of you know odd  system but they watch women so the mit  team  would recruit as many women as they  could and this was actually much harder  for these guys to do  if you knew these guys you'd know what i  was saying but they would actually end  up hiring women they would hire  strippers to sit at the table as a  distractor to keep the cameras on the  woman and they'd be betting ten thousand  dollars a hand  or they would also sit at tables where  there were real high rollers like  celebrities because if there's a  celebrity at your table even if he's  only betting a hundred dollars a hand  the cameras are all on him and you can  be sitting here betting ten thousand  dollars and nobody cares  and so they've played with all of the  celebrities it's funny as we made the  movie  i mean we had played with kevin spacey  before we knew kevin spacey and people  like  you know lawrence fishburne had been  sitting at the table before but they had  no idea that mit kids were sitting with  them  so that was kind of cool but anyways  that was that system and that was that  book  now rigged you know which is the book  the new one that's out now um  it came about basically after bringing  down the house came out i knew this kid  who had gone to harvard business school  and uh his real name is john dagistino  and he actually let me put his real name  in the beginning of the book  but not in the whole book and i'll get  into that a little later but um john was  a kid who went to harvard business  school and i was friends with his  girlfriend  and john was only remarkable to me and  that he was this most intense guy i'd  ever met  incredibly ambitious really intense one  of these guys whose hair is always  perfect and his suit is always perfect  he's you know he's got himself together  he's very you know  if you know hbs guys he looked like an  hbs guy  um basically i lost track of him and a  couple years later he called me up and  he invited me to ring the bell  to open the something called the merck  exchange to ring the morning bell  i had never heard of the merc exchange i  didn't know anything about oil i don't  know anything about the mark exchange i  knew it was in new york  but that was it so i went over to new  york and i got to this place and  it was that pit that you see in the  movie trading places  you know where people are going crazy  and yelling at each other s